.TH OWBOX 1 "2026" "owbox 0.3.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
owbox \- a stacking Wayland compositor based on Openbox
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B owbox
[\fIOPTION\fR]...
.br
.B owbox-session
[\fIOPTION\fR]...
.br
.B owbox-screenshot
[\fBscreen\fR|\fBarea\fR|\fBwindow\fR]
.br
.B owbox-volume
\fBup\fR|\fBdown\fR|\fBmute\fR|\fBmic-mute\fR
.br
.B owbox-brightness
\fBup\fR|\fBdown\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B owbox
is a Wayland compositor built from Openbox's window management code.  It
reads Openbox's configuration files, themes and menus, and behaves like
Openbox, key and mouse bindings included.  X applications run through
Xwayland.  owbox is an independent project, not Openbox, and isn't
affiliated with the Openbox developers: report problems with it to owbox.
.PP
Start it from a display manager (the \fBowbox\fR session) or from a text
console with \fBowbox-session\fR, which reads the environment files first.
Run inside another Wayland or X session, it opens a window of its own.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-help
Display the help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Display the version and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-config\-file " FILE"
Use FILE as rc.xml.
.TP
.BI \-\-startup " CMD"
Run CMD after starting.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-autostart
Don't run the autostart script and the XDG autostart applications.
.TP
.B \-\-reconfigure
Tell the running owbox to reload its configuration.
.TP
.B \-\-restart
The same as \-\-reconfigure: a Wayland compositor can't restart without
closing its windows.
.TP
.B \-\-exit
Tell the running owbox to exit.
.TP
.B \-\-choose\-share
Show the menu of monitors and windows to share and print the choice, for
xdg\-desktop\-portal\-wlr.
.TP
.BI \-\-msg " COMMAND"
Send a command to the running owbox and print the reply, see
\fBCOMMANDS\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Print debugging messages.
.TP
.B \-\-debug\-focus
Print debugging messages about focus.
.TP
.B \-\-debug\-wlroots
Print wlroots' debugging messages.
.SH CONFIGURATION
\fBowbox\-settings\fR changes the settings in a window.
owbox reads Openbox's files.  Each is looked for in
\fI~/.config/owbox\fR, then \fI~/.config/openbox\fR, then the same
directories under each of \fB$XDG_CONFIG_DIRS\fR (\fI/etc/xdg\fR):
.TP
.I rc.xml
The configuration, see
.UR http://openbox.org/wiki/Help:Configuration
.UE .
owbox's additions are in an \fB<owbox>\fR section, which Openbox ignores;
the installed rc.xml describes them.  \fB<owbox><scale>\fR draws window
frames, menus and popups larger than the theme, applications keep their
size.  The file is reloaded when it changes.
.TP
.I menu.xml
The menus.  owbox's built\-in \fBapplications\-menu\fR lists the installed
applications by category.
.TP
.I autostart
A shell script run when owbox starts (only from the owbox directories,
Openbox's autostart usually starts X programs).  Applications in the XDG
autostart directories are started too.
.TP
.I environment
Shell variable assignments read by \fBowbox\-session\fR, which also
points \fBSSH_AUTH_SOCK\fR at the SSH agent systemd started.
.PP
Themes are Openbox themes, found in \fI~/.local/share/themes\fR,
\fI~/.themes\fR and \fI/usr/share/themes\fR (\fINAME/openbox\-3/themerc\fR).
.SH COMMANDS
\fBowbox \-\-msg\fR sends a command over owbox's socket
(\fB$OWBOX_SOCK\fR, set for programs owbox runs).  The reply starts with
\fBok\fR or \fBerror\fR.
.TP
.B reconfigure\fR, \fBexit
As the options.
.TP
.BI action " XML"
Run Openbox actions, written like in rc.xml, for example:
.br
owbox \-\-msg 'action <action name="GoToDesktop"><to>2</to></action>'
.TP
.B windows
The windows, one JSON object per line, bottom to top.
.TP
.B choose\-share
Show the menu of monitors and windows to share, and reply with the choice
(also \fBowbox \-\-choose\-share\fR).
.TP
.B desktops
The desktops and the current one, as JSON.
.TP
.B outputs
The monitors, one JSON object per line.
.TP
.B config\-file
The path of the rc.xml owbox loaded.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
owbox sets \fBWAYLAND_DISPLAY\fR, \fBDISPLAY\fR (for X applications),
\fBXDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP\fR=owbox (if not set), \fBXDG_SESSION_TYPE\fR and
\fBOWBOX_SOCK\fR for the programs it runs, and passes them to D\-Bus and
systemd.  It starts \fBowbox\-session.target\fR (bound to
\fBgraphical\-session.target\fR) and stops it when it exits.
.SH PANELS
Tapping Super (pressing and releasing it alone) shows the panels (bars
along the screen's edges, like waybar) above the dimmed windows, and a
launcher (\fBowbox\-launcher\fR, which runs fuzzel or another installed
one), until Escape, a click elsewhere, or switching to a window.
\fB<owbox><panels>\fR in rc.xml can hide the panels the rest of the time.
Example configurations for waybar and fuzzel are in
\fI/usr/share/owbox/examples\fR.
.SH IDLE AND LOCKING
The monitors turn off after ten minutes without input, unless a window asks
to keep them on, and the screen is locked then, before suspending, and on
\fBloginctl lock\-session\fR (the menu's Lock Screen), with
\fBswaylock\fR(1) or another installed screen locker.
\fB<owbox><idle>\fR in rc.xml sets it.
.PP
\fBowbox\-volume\fR and \fBowbox\-brightness\fR, which the volume and
brightness keys run, change the level and show it in a notification.
.SH SCREENSHOTS
\fBowbox\-screenshot\fR saves a screenshot with \fBgrim\fR(1) in
\fIPictures/Screenshots\fR and copies it to the clipboard: of every
monitor (\fBscreen\fR, the default), of an area chosen with
\fBslurp\fR(1) (\fBarea\fR), or of the focused window (\fBwindow\fR).
The default rc.xml binds it to Print, Shift+Print and Alt+Print.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.cache/owbox/owbox.log
The log of the last run.
.PP
When owbox runs on a console, the messages of the programs it starts go to
the systemd journal, under the identifier \fBowbox\fR
(\fBjournalctl \-t owbox \-b\fR).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR openbox (1)
